    "type": "custom",
    "value": [
      "When the letters N and G come at the end of a word, they make one new sound — the humming sound at the end of ‘song’.",
      "And here's the special part: that sound GLUES itself to the vowel right before it. The vowel and the N-G stick together into one chunk, like ‘-ong’ in ‘song’ or ‘-ung’ in ‘sung’.",
      "N and K do the same gluing trick — like ‘-onk’ in ‘honk’ and ‘-unk’ in ‘trunk’.",
      "When you see these chunks, don't pull them apart. Read the whole chunk as one glued sound."
    ]
  },
